cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LOCI in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LOCI: Spatial Memory for Physical AI"
abstract: >-
  LOCI is a 4D spatiotemporal vector memory for world models and embodied
  agents. Every memory carries an (x, y, z, t) address indexed with
  multi-resolution Hilbert bucketing, so robots, drones and world models can
  retrieve what they perceived by similarity, place and time, reconstruct
  trajectories, and score how novel a predicted future is.
authors:
  - family-names: Dyras
    given-names: Zygmunt
repository-code: "https://github.com/zd87pl/loci-db"
url: "https://github.com/zd87pl/loci-db"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
keywords:
  - physical AI
  - embodied AI
  - robotics
  - spatial memory
  - world models
  - vector database
  - spatiotemporal indexing
  - Hilbert curve
  - novelty detection
